# OpenCode commands

The root `just opencode` recipe links this directory to `~/.config/opencode/commands/`. OpenCode discovers `.md` files as slash commands and reloads them automatically. This README and the reference files deliberately have no `.md` suffix, so they do not become commands.

## /split

Install with `just opencode`, then run `/split` in an OpenCode session inside a Herdr tab. It forks the current conversation in the same working directory, reports the new session ID, and tells the fork to wait for instructions.

The Herdr app adds the fork to the right of the last pane in the same tab, not necessarily beside the pane where you ran `/split`. The command uses `uv`, `opencode` with its shared local service, and `hc` on the machine running OpenCode. No desktop socket forwarding is needed.

## /retro

Run `/retro` to review the current coding session, or `/retro <session log or focus>` to specify another session or a focus. It proposes improvements to the agent's environment, ordered by severity, and waits for your selection before changing anything. It runs in the current session so it can use the conversation history.

Source attribution, acquisition details, pinned upstream links, and adaptations are recorded in `retro.md` under the YAML frontmatter's `metadata.provenance` field.

### Updating the upstream copy

Choose an upstream commit, read the source files listed in `metadata.provenance.sources` at that revision, and compare them with the local copies. Preserve the documented OpenCode adaptations and license notice. Update the provenance metadata when refreshing the copy.
